+# FSRESTModuleImpl
+
+## Module Information
+
+- **Package**: `io.github.eipx.remoteagent.modules.core.FSRESTModuleImpl`
+- **Extends**: `AbstractStoppableModule`
+- **Implements**: `BaseModule`, `RESTNamespaceHandler`
+- **Type**: <span class='badge-core'>Core</span>
+- **REST Namespace**: `/agent/sessions/{sessionToken}/fs`
+- **Session Required**: <span class='badge-yes'>YES</span>
+- **Dependencies**: [RESTModuleImpl](/modules/RESTModuleImpl), [FSModuleImpl](/modules/FSModuleImpl)
+
+## Description
+
+`FSRESTModuleImpl` is the REST entry point for the file system (FS) module.
+The SOAP endpoint of `FSModuleImpl` is published with `requireSession = true`
+(its constructor passes the flag to the RPC base class, so the SOAP context
+carries the session filter and a call without a valid session cookie gets `401`).
+The REST namespace is therefore registered the same way,
+`registerNamespace("fs", this, true)` on [RESTModuleImpl](/modules/RESTModuleImpl):
+the core mounts it under `/agent/sessions/{sessionToken}/fs`, resolves the session
+token once and delegates every request to this module together with the session,
+which the file operations do not otherwise use. The handlers invoke the public
+methods of [FSModuleImpl](/modules/FSModuleImpl), the same domain logic used by
+the SOAP (JAX-WS) entry point.
+
+Paths travel URL-encoded in the `path` query parameter and are interpreted
+exactly as SOAP interprets them (absolute operating-system paths; no
+normalization or restriction beyond what the domain applies).
+
+## Activation
+
+`FSModuleImpl` is part of the default module list, and so is this module:
+
+```properties
+Agent.modules=internal.DiagnosticsModule;core.FSModuleImpl;core.FSRESTModuleImpl;core.ProcessModuleImpl;core.RESTModuleImpl;
+```
+
+Remove `core.FSRESTModuleImpl` from the list to keep the SOAP interface only.
+
+## REST Routes (`/agent/sessions/{sessionToken}/fs`)
+
+| Method | Path | Handler | SOAP Equivalent | Description |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `GET` | `/fs/entries?path=` | `handleStat` | `fileExists`, `directoryExists`, `fileSize` | Existence, type and size in one call |
+| `GET` | `/fs/files?path=[&offset=&length=]` | `handleReadFile` | `readEntireFile`, `readFile` | Read the whole file, or a window of it |
+| `PUT` | `/fs/files?path=` | `handleWriteFile` | `writeFile` | Create or fully overwrite a file (body: `application/octet-stream`) |
+| `DELETE` | `/fs/files?path=` | `handleRemoveFile` | `removeFile` | Delete a file |
+| `POST` | `/fs/files/copy` | `handleCopyFile` | `copyFile` | Copy a file (body: `{"source","destination"}`) |
+| `POST` | `/fs/files/move` | `handleMoveFile` | `moveFile` | Move or rename a file or directory (body: `{"source","destination"}`) |
+| `GET` | `/fs/directories?path=` | `handleListDirectory` | `listDirectory` | List directory entries |
+| `PUT` | `/fs/directories?path=` | `handleMakeDirectory` | `makeDirectory` | Create a directory (parent must exist) |
+| `DELETE` | `/fs/directories?path=` | `handleRemoveDirectory` | `removeDirectory` | Remove an empty directory |
+
+Method choice follows HTTP semantics: reads and existence checks are `GET`
+(safe), full overwrite and "make directory" are `PUT` (idempotent), deletes are
+`DELETE`, and copy/move are `POST` actions because repeating them can change
+the outcome.
+
+## Query Parameters
+
+| Parameter | Routes | Description |
+|---|---|---|
+| `path` | all except `copy`/`move` | Absolute path, URL-encoded; required |
+| `offset` | `GET /fs/files` | Byte offset to start reading from; default `0`; must be `>= 0` |
+| `length` | `GET /fs/files` | Number of bytes to read; omit for the whole file; must be `>= 1` |
+
+## Request Bodies
+
+- `PUT /fs/files`: the raw file content as `application/octet-stream`. An empty
+  body writes an empty file, as SOAP allows.
+- `POST /fs/files/copy`, `POST /fs/files/move`:
+
+```json
+{ "source": "/path/to/source", "destination": "/path/to/destination" }
+```
+
+## Response Bodies
+
+- `GET /fs/entries`: `{"path", "exists", "type": "file"|"directory"|"none", "readable", "size"}`
+  (`readable` and `size` only for files; `size` only when readable).
+- `GET /fs/files`: the file content as `application/octet-stream`.
+- `GET /fs/directories`: `{"path", "entries": [...]}`.
+- `PUT /fs/files`: `{"success": true, "bytes": n}`.
+- Other state changes: `{"success": true}`.
+
+## Response Codes
+
+| Code | Condition |
+|---|---|
+| `200` | Read succeeded; state change applied to an existing entry (overwrite, delete, move, directory already present) |
+| `201` | File or directory created; copy written (`Location` header set) |
+| `400` | Missing `path`, invalid `offset`/`length`, malformed JSON body, malformed `Content-Length` |
+| `403` | Entry exists but is not readable (read) or not writable (overwrite, delete) |
+| `404` | Entry does not exist, or is not of the named kind (a directory where a file is expected and vice versa); unknown route |
+| `405` | Path exists but HTTP method not supported |
+| `409` | Operation cannot be applied to the current state: parent directory missing, directory not empty or not writable, destination occupied |
+| `413` | File or body larger than `FSRESTModuleImpl.maxFileSize` (reads can page with `offset`/`length`) |
+| `500` | I/O error raised by the domain (surfaces as a SOAP fault on the SOAP path) |
+
+`GET /fs/entries` never returns `404`: `"exists": false` is the answer, exactly
+as `fileExists` returns `false`.
+
+## Configuration
+
+| Property | Type | Default | Description |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `FSRESTModuleImpl.maxFileSize` | long | `67108864` | Largest file payload accepted (`PUT`) or returned whole (`GET` without `length`), in bytes; larger requests receive `413`. |
+
+## Key Components
+
+| Component | Description |
+|---|---|
+| `RESTNamespaceHandler` | Interface implemented to receive requests for a registered namespace (the core resolves the session before delegating) |
+| `RESTRouter` | Shared route/dispatch utility (`Route<Void>` table) |
+| `FSModuleImpl` | Public domain methods invoked by the handlers |
+| `RESTUtil` | Query parsing, JSON parsing, JSON/binary response helpers |
+
+## Summary
+
+- **Transport**: HTTP/1.1 (shared `HttpServer` via `RESTModuleImpl`)
+- **Message Format**: Raw bytes for file content; JSON control envelopes
+- **Dependencies**: 2 (RESTModuleImpl, FSModuleImpl)
+- **Session Scope**: required, for parity with the SOAP endpoint; not used by the operations
